{"tanyekavacanadvivacanabahuvacananyekasaH": [{"id": "tAnyekavacanadvivacanabahuvacanAnyekaSaH", "headword": "तान्येकवचनद्विवचनबहुवचनान्येकशः", "headword_slp1": "tAnyekavacanadvivacanabahuvacanAnyekaSaH", "fold": "tanyekavacanadvivacanabahuvacananyekasaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "These three triads of conjugational affixes, which have received the name of Lowest etc. are called (as regard the three expressions in each triad) severally 'the expression for one' (singular), 'the expression for two' (dual) and 'the expression for many' (plural).\n\nTerms:", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["तान्येकवचनद्विवचनबहुवचनान्येकशः १.४.१०२", "१.४.१०२", "१.४.१०२ तान्येकवचनद्विवचनबहुवचनान्येकशः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["tAnyekavacanadvivacanabahuvacanAnyekaSaH १.४.१०२", "१.४.१०२", "१.४.१०२ tAnyekavacanadvivacanabahuvacanAnyekaSaH"]}], "tanadiByastaTasoH": [{"id": "tanAdiByastaTAsoH", "headword": "तनादिभ्यस्तथासोः", "headword_slp1": "tanAdiByastaTAsoH", "fold": "tanadiByastaTasoH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After the verbs तन् 'to expand' and others there is optionally the लुक् elision of सिच् when the आत्मनेपद affixes त and थास् of the 2nd Person follow.\n\nTerms: सिच्-elision", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["तनादिभ्यस्तथासोः २.४.७९", "२.४.७९", "२.४.७९ तनादिभ्यस्तथासोः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["tanAdiByastaTAsoH २.४.७९", "२.४.७९", "२.४.७९ tanAdiByastaTAsoH"]}], "tanukaraRe taksaH": [{"id": "tanUkaraRe takzaH", "headword": "तनूकरणे तक्षः", "headword_slp1": "tanUkaraRe takzaH", "fold": "tanukaraRe taksaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix श्यन् is optionally used after the root अक्ष् 'to bore or hew' when it is preceded by the preposition सम् and when a सार्वधातुक affix denoting an agent, follows. \n\nTerms: श्नु", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["तनूकरणे तक्षः ३.१.७६", "३.१.७६", "३.१.७६ तनूकरणे तक्ष