tituted for the final of तन् before the Passive characteristic यक्।\n\nTerms: अभीय Rules", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["तनोतेर्यकि ६.४.४४", "६.४.४४", "६.४.४४ तनोतेर्यकि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["tanoteryaki ६.४.४४", "६.४.४४", "६.४.४४ tanoteryaki"]}], "tanipatyosCandasi": [{"id": "tanipatyoSCandasi", "headword": "तनिपत्योश्छन्दसि", "headword_slp1": "tanipatyoSCandasi", "fold": "tanipatyosCandasi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the root-vowel of तन् and पत् is elided before an affix beginning with a vowel, when it has an indicatory क् or ङ् ।\n\nTerms: कित् and ङित्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["तनिपत्योश्छन्दसि ६.४.९९", "६.४.९९", "६.४.९९ तनिपत्योश्छन्दसि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["tanipatyoSCandasi ६.४.९९", "६.४.९९", "६.४.९९ tanipatyoSCandasi"]}]}